{
  "type": "say",
  "text": "Thank you all for those critical inputs. Let me summarize what I'm hearing before I make my decision. Ravi, the retrofit is mandatory on safety grounds — not optional — and requires 6 hours of energized lockout plus post-update safety-I/O validation. The vendor bulletin still needs to be attached to the work order. Marta, Cell 4 can cover 160 of the 240 assemblies but the reservation expires Thursday at noon and isn't yet in the system, so we need to lock that in today. The remaining 80 must run on Cell 5 post-retrofit. Jonah, the first 20 assemblies after the firmware change must be quarantined for validation, which means only 60 of the 80 Cell 5 assemblies would be available for release to the Friday order — leaving us 20 short of the 240 requirement. So here's what I need to resolve before authorizing: Marta, can Cell 4 produce more than 160, or can we adjust the split so Cell 5 only needs to produce 60 post-retrofit assemblies — 20 for validation hold and 40 for release? That would still leave us short. Alternatively, can the Friday order deadline accommodate partial shipment, or do we need to find additional capacity? I need a clear path to 240 releasable assemblies before I can authorize this work."
}
```

